$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}(x+y)(x-y)|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}uv\\cdot |-\\frac{1}{2}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{∬}_{Δ}uv\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u[{\\int }_{2}^{4}v\\,dv]du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u{[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{2}^{4}\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}u(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})\\,du \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}u\\,du \\\\  & =3[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
